From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 07:53:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(turns): a provider's own line for the user ends the
 turn as is

When every Claude account in the pool was at its weekly limit, the pool raised one plain line ("All Claude accounts are at their limit ..."), yet the turn still went through the generic error path: it retried, then ended with "Rate limited after 3 retries" and the "Provider said:" copy around the line, or around the raw upstream error with its status code and request id.

A provider error may now carry `hermes_user_message`: one plain sentence for the user, set by a provider that has already done every retry it can (an account pool with no account left). The turn then ends at once with that line as its whole reply and error: no retries, no fallback, the buffered retry chatter dropped, the raw error only in the log. `hermes_resets_at` (epoch seconds, optional) becomes `failure_resets_at`. The line is also found on a wrapped cause. Errors without it keep today's path. No new key.
---
